      "sourceText": "这就是下坡尤其要看的地方：正常坡的较低侧，可能只是低于这一小片的代表地面，并不是真正的坑。反过来，真正坑洼只有被雷达看到且留下有效回波，才可能通过这个高度差表现出来；没有回波的断崖不因此自动得到可靠识别。扩展节点也没有近场那种 `noDataObstacle` 合成障碍功能，没有点的区域如何影响规划，还取决于下游的未知区域设置。",
      "translatedText": "This is especially what to look at on a downhill slope: the lower side of a normal slope may simply be the representative ground lower than this small patch, and is not a true pit\\. Conversely, a true depression can be represented through this height difference only if it is seen by radar and leaves a valid echo; a cliff with no echo does not automatically become reliably identified because of this\\. The expansion node also does not have the near\\-field `noDataObstacle` synthetic obstacle function; how areas without points affect planning still depends on the downstream unknown\\-area settings\\.",
      "provider": "deepseek",
      "model": "deepseek-flash",
      "usage": {
        "inputTokens": 217,
        "outputTokens": 114,
        "costUsd": 0.000202
      }
